","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99569","id":2495529723,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UvsL7","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T16:24:03Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T16:24:57Z","body":"> I like the idea, but I'd say this would be better suited to the **View** menu at the top of the 3D editor viewport instead. This way, it'll persist on a per-scene basis and behave more like the other gizmo visibility options which are present in that menu.\r\n\r\nPersonally I know I will probably never have this option enabled. So having to set it per scene would be tedious IMO.  Especially when importing many meshes and viewing their scenes.  But if that's the recommended way forward I can make that change as I'd rather have the option than none at all. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495529723/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495672509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99569#issuecomment-2495672509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99569","id":2495672509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UwPC9","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T22:24:39Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T01:09:44Z","body":"@Calinou \r\n\r\nSo after exploring some I'm running into issues of how to connect that view menu setting to the gizmo logic.  without access to the scene's state I can't look up that property.  \r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1825a67-0016-4b90-a3e1-088d850dbf48)\r\n\r\n\r\n One solution I have found is adding a fourth option to the gizmo visibility selector:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/163b1c53-cbba-4ec2-845b-421a779095e5)\r\n\r\nand then replace this check with the following:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0c45ace151f25de2ca54fe7a46b6f077be32ba6f/editor/plugins/node_3d_editor_gizmos.cpp#L1062\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nref->set_hidden(current_state == HIDDEN || (!ref->is_selected() && current_state == SELECTED));\r\n```\r\n\r\nThoughts on this vs the current PR in the Editor Settings/Editors/3d Gizmos/Gizmo Settings?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495672509/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510377608","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99569#issuecomment-2510377608","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99569","id":2510377608,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VoVKI","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-02T01:26:23Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T14:35:41Z","body":"Sorry was away on holiday, hopefully this is more clear. The issue I was running into regarding putting it in the view menu, is how to access that property. Since it is stored within the editstate file of the scene itself. \r\n\r\n  I can't find a clean way of accessing  `Node3DEditorViewport:: view_menu->get_popup()->is_item_checked(...)` from `CollisionShape3DGizmoPlugin::redraw`\r\n\r\nas far as I can see the only route of communication between those settings is via https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/893bbdfde8ad1f94fb4e6db246ff7075569396ea/editor/plugins/node_3d_editor_gizmos.cpp#L1046\r\n\r\nwhich is where the visibility selection is checked. \r\n\r\n### Solution 1:\r\nCurrent PR, adding a new setting within  `editors/3d_gizmos/gizmo_settings/always_show_collision_shapes`\r\nIMO the least bloat and my preferred solution.\r\n\r\n### Solution 2:\r\nadding a fourth option to the gizmo visiblity for only visible while selected (applies to all gizmos): \r\nThis would require some modification to change VISIBLE = ALWAYS VISIBLE, and setting defaults for gizmos to whatever they are now.  ex: Light3DGizmo is selected only, Collision is always. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/893bbdfde8ad1f94fb4e6db246ff7075569396ea/editor/plugins/node_3d_editor_gizmos.h#L153-L156\r\n\r\n\r\n### Solution 3:\r\nExposing something akin to EDITOR_GET for the scenes edit state. or pulling the state with something like this:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n\tNode3DEditorViewport *vp = Node3DEditor::get_singleton()->get_last_used_viewport();\r\n\tDictionary d = vp->get_state();\r\n\tif (d.has(\"always_show_collision_shapes\")) {\r\n\t\tshow_collision_shapes_always = d[\"always_show_collision_shapes\"];\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut this feels rather messy\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510377608/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563140355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99569#issuecomment-2563140355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99569","id":2563140355,"n